  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Name 5 different types of human teeth and explain their functions. List some measures to prevent tooth decay, which is commonly seen in Bhutan, especially in school-going children. (3 marks)', 'Types: (1) incisors - chisel-shaped front teeth for cutting and biting food; (2) canines - pointed teeth for tearing; (3) premolars - for crushing and grinding; (4) molars - broad teeth for grinding and chewing; (5) third molars (wisdom teeth) - extra grinding teeth at the back. Prevention of tooth decay: brush twice a day with fluoride toothpaste and clean between teeth; reduce sugary snacks, sweets and soft drinks and avoid chewing doma (betel nut); rinse the mouth after meals; drink safe water; visit a dental clinic regularly for check-ups, fluoride varnish and fissure sealants; and support school oral health education and supervised tooth-brushing programmes.', null, '[{"point": "Types and functions: incisors (cutting/ biting), canines (tearing), premolars (crushing/ grinding), molars (grinding), wisdom teeth (third molars - grinding)", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Prevention: brush twice daily with fluoride toothpaste, floss, limit sugary food/ drinks/ doma, rinse after meals, regular dental check-ups, school oral health programmes, fissure sealants/ fluoride varnish", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
