  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Among many public health issues in Bhutan, alcohol liver disease (ALD) tops the list; Jigme Dorji Wangchuck National Referral Hospital in Thimphu reports the highest deaths every year due to ALD.
(a) Explain briefly how the consumption of alcohol causes ALD.
(b) Write down at least 5 of the most important measures you would suggest to discourage the consumption of alcohol in Bhutan. (3 marks)', '(a) The liver metabolises alcohol; this produces toxic acetaldehyde and free radicals and changes fat metabolism. With regular heavy drinking, fat accumulates in liver cells (fatty liver), then inflammation and cell death occur (alcoholic hepatitis), and repeated injury causes scarring (fibrosis) leading to cirrhosis, with liver failure, jaundice, ascites, bleeding varices and liver cancer. (b) Measures: increase taxes and prices of alcohol; reduce availability - fewer bar licences, limited opening hours and dry days; enforce the minimum legal drinking age and drink-driving laws; ban alcohol advertising and promotion; regulate home brewing of ara; public awareness and school education on harms; screening and brief interventions in health facilities; treatment, counselling and rehabilitation services; involve communities, religious leaders and families.', null, '[{"point": "(a) Liver metabolises alcohol to toxic acetaldehyde and free radicals → fatty liver (steatosis) → alcoholic hepatitis (inflammation) → fibrosis and cirrhosis (liver failure, portal hypertension)", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "(b) Five measures: higher taxes/ prices, restrict sale hours/ outlets/ licences, enforce age limits and drink-driving laws, ban advertising, awareness campaigns, control home brewing (ara), screening and brief interventions, treatment/ rehabilitation, community and religious involvement", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
