  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'What is the 5S approach used in health facilities? Explain each of the five S''s and give two benefits of 5S in a hospital. (3 marks)', '5S is a workplace organisation method from Japanese management used as the base for continuous quality improvement (CQI) in health facilities. (1) Sort (Seiri) - remove items that are not needed; (2) Set in order (Seiton) - arrange needed items so they are easy to find and return, with labels; (3) Shine (Seiso) - clean the workplace and equipment and inspect for problems; (4) Standardise (Seiketsu) - make the first three S''s routine with standard procedures, signs and checklists; (5) Sustain (Shitsuke) - build the habit and discipline through training, monitoring and audits. Benefits: a cleaner, safer and more organised workplace; less time wasted searching for items; fewer errors and expired drugs; better infection control; efficient use of space; and improved patient and staff satisfaction and quality of care.', null, '[{"point": "Five S''s: Sort (remove unneeded items), Set in order (a place for everything, labelled), Shine (clean and inspect), Standardise (common rules/ procedures), Sustain (discipline, habit, audits)", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Benefits (any two): safer, cleaner workplace, less time searching, fewer errors/ expired items, better infection control, efficient use of space, improved patient and staff satisfaction, basis for CQI", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
